   807	The kernel of a homomorphism $\alpha:A\to B$ of abelian varieties is the fibre
   808	over $0$ in the sense of algebraic spaces.  The homomorphism $\alpha$ is an
   809	isogeny if it is surjective and has finite kernel.  Its degree is its degree as
   810	a regular map.  Write $A_n=\ker(n_A)$ for the $n$-torsion group scheme.
   811	\end{definition}
